{"name":"The Ego Has Landed","hex":"#a75455","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ego","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Eggon."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The self, especially with a sense of self-importance.","The most central part of the mind, which mediates with one's surroundings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ego"},{"term":"has","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Haisla."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of have"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/has"},{"term":"landed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In possession of land.","Consisting of land, especially with a single owner."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of land"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landed"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Ego Has Landed","blocks":[{"text":"The Ego Has Landed is a compilation album by English singer Robbie Williams. After his success around the world, especially in Europe, Williams was signed to Capitol Records in the United States, which was a part of EMI at the time. The album was released in May 1999 in the United States and Canada, and later issued worldwide. All tracks were previously released on Williams' first two albums, Life thru a Lens (1997) and I've Been Expecting You (1998)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/The_Ego_Has_Landed_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ego_Has_Landed"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"ego":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ego.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%2